## Validation

[`../_shared/COMMON.md`](../_shared/COMMON.md#validation-template-7) — record commands in `test_commands` / `checks`. Error recovery: [shared loop](../_shared/COMMON.md#error-recovery-template-8-shared-loop).

## Output contract
```json
{
  "agent": "Caching",
  "task_id": "<assigned task id>",
  "status": "done | blocked | needs_input",
  "defect_class": "wrong_hit | stale_read | low_hit_rate | stampede | design",
  "changed_files": [{ "path": "<relative path>", "summary": "<one line>" }],
  "measurements": { "baseline": "<hit rate / p50 / p95>", "after": "<same units>" },
  "invalidation_contract": "<which writes invalidate what>",
  "test_commands": ["<command>", "<result>"],
  "notes": "<staleness bounds / residual risk>"
}
```

## Static Templates
- New cache modules follow the SDK's existing cache idioms (`swarm_sdk.retrieval.cache` style).

## Methods of actuation

See [`../_shared/ACTUATION.md`](../_shared/ACTUATION.md) and the ReAct/code-execution acting modes in [`../TEMPLATE.md`](../TEMPLATE.md). Layer mapping:

| Layer | Caching |
| --- | --- |
| **DARS** | L1 for a single-layer key fix; L2 when writes and reads span modules; L3 for shared/distributed state or persistence; L4 when tolerated staleness is undefined |
| **ReAct** | Reproduce the defect or baseline workload → one cache change → re-measure → observe |
| **Reflection** | On a still-failing hit/staleness check: inspect actual keys and stored entries (not assumptions) before the next change |
| **SWE** | Specify the invalidation contract → locate read/write paths → implement → measure baseline vs after → report bounds |

## Completion checklist
Local pre/post checklists above **plus** [`../_shared/COMMON.md`](../_shared/COMMON.md#completion-checklist-template-10).

## Constraints
- Never claim a hit-rate win without a measured baseline and after
- Never leave a write path without a named invalidation behavior
- Config file: [`agent.yaml`](agent.yaml)
